<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Alfonso III of Asturias</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">c. 848–<a href="/years/910">910</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> · Also known as Alfonso the Great</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Alfonso III, called the Great, was King of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/asturias">Asturias</a> from 866 to 910. His <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/vassal">vassals</a> took <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/porto">Porto</a> in 868 and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/coimbra">Coimbra</a> in 878, extending Christian settlement to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/douro">Douro</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/mondego">Mondego</a> and creating the counties of Portugal and Coimbra. Chronicles written at his court shaped the idea of the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/reconquista">Reconquista</a>, and after him the capital moved to León.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alfonso-iii-of-asturias.jpg" alt="Alfonso III of Asturias" width="320" height="484" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Pelagius · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Testamento.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
